{
  "abstract": "In parameter-free RMSNorm (`weight=None`) Pre-Norm Transformers trained at zero learning-rate warmup (`WARMUP_RATIO = 0.0`, `MATRIX_LR = 0.04`) with `MuonAdamW` (`50.3M` Depth-8 and `26.35M` Depth-6 GPT, 953 updates = 499.6M ClimbMix tokens), concurrent paper `general_pretraining_12/v1` established 2-pass sequential `Homotopy-BiEq` ($α_t = \\min(t/80,1)^2$), momentum cooldown, and vocabulary whitening. Complementing `general_pretraining_12/v1` without overlapping its optimizer claims, we report three non-overlapping diagnostic findings across 45 runs (`44` hash-verified workspace runs + `reference_seed42`). First, in the measured PyTorch `2.9.1+cu126` / `TorchInductor` graph, naive unfused pre-sublayer channel scaling retains `97` vs. `93` full `(B,T,d)` `bfloat16` storages (`+256.0 MiB` at `B=32`, `+512.0 MiB` at `B=64`) because the 32-channel gate slice view `ve_gate(x[..., :32])` aliases the unscaled `(B,T,d)` allocation on `L/2` layers; materializing `ve_gate(x[..., :32].contiguous())` restores `93` `(B,T,d)` storages (`+16.0/+32.0 MiB`), and online weight-column fusion ($W \\odot \\mathbf{1}\\alpha^\\top$) eliminates extra activation buffers entirely (`+0.08 MiB` VRAM). Second, across both Linear (`exp07, exp03, exp05`) and Stopped-Exponential (`exp07, exp64, exp17`) $2 \\times 2$ factorials on Seed 47, post-QK-norm scaling (`+2,048` scalars) accounts for `73.9%–93.5%` (`-0.001563` to `-0.002300` BPB) of the combined gain while weight-fused pre-sublayer gains (`+8,192` scalars) add `-0.000550` to `-0.000572` BPB; we prove directly on discrete positions ($\\det(R(2\\theta_c)-I_2)=4\\sin^2(\\theta_c)>0$) that RoPE pair tying is necessary and sufficient for unit-shift stationarity over all content vectors, while 3-seed standalone comparisons against `4,096`-scalar untied `nGPT` (`0.993133 ± 0.000446` vs. `0.993279 ± 0.000471` BPB) show that the primary `~0.00183–0.00197` BPB gain is shared. Third, in common-backbone 3-seed pre-polar adaptations, `Zeta` (`0.994766 ± 0.001892` BPB, `+96 MiB`) and `Undamped BiEq` (`0.993841 ± 0.002193` BPB) drive `Seed 137` skip weights `x0_lambdas` monotonically negative during Steps 10–80 under `WARMUP_RATIO = 0.0`, `Turbo-Muon` reaches `0.993090 ± 0.000621` BPB vs. `0.992605 ± 0.000371` (`BF16`) and `0.992584 ± 0.000356` (`FP32`) for `Homotopy-BiEq`, and square attention matrices account for `52.1%` (`exp47`) vs. `47.9%` from rectangular MLP/gate matrices.",
